{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, בְּאֵשׁ","hw":"בְּאֵשׁ","html":"† <big><big><span dir=\"rtl\">בְּאֵשׁ</span></big></big>  <strong>vb. be evil, bad (</strong>so 𝔗; Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܒܶܐܫ</span>; Old Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">באש</span> Lzb <sup>233</sup> SAC <sup>27</sup> Cooke <sup>191</sup>; cf.BH<strong>)</strong>;—<br><strong>Pe.</strong>  Pf. 3 ms. impers. <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳ עֲלוֹהִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:15\" href=\"/Daniel.6.15\">Dn 6:15</a> i.e. <em>it was evil</em> (<em>displeasing</em>) <em>to him</em> (cf.BH [<a data-ref=\"BDB, רעע\" href=\"/BDB,_רעע\", dir=\"rtl\">רעע</a>] <strong>1</strong>).","next":"BDB Aramaic, בִּאישׁ","prev":"BDB Aramaic, בְּ"}